From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845-xiaomi-polaris: disable unsupported QCE

Linux 7.3 marks CRYPTO_DEV_QCE as BROKEN: the driver cannot arbitrate
access with the secure world and is slower than the CPU. No driver binds
the SoC crypto node, yet it defaults to enabled and consumes GCC CE1
clocks, so fw_devlink keeps the GCC sync_state() pending for the whole
boot and genpd keeps every GDSC that was on at boot powered on.
Disable this Linux consumer on the board; leave the remote-controlled
BAM and secure-world ownership untouched. CPU crypto remains available.
Do not override BROKEN.

This mirrors the Xiaomi Aurora (SM8650) board change.

Reference: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v7.3-rc6/drivers/crypto/Kconfig

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-polaris.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-polaris.dts
@@ -395,6 +395,10 @@
 &cdsp_pas {
 	firmware-name = "qcom/sdm845/Xiaomi/polaris/cdsp.mbn";
 
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&crypto {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
